# POLLY, writing a song (the second UX pass's fixes): REC's screen offers a pattern as long as the loop (its bars
# repeated into the new ones); a pattern's bars changed while a loop plays stay in step with the loop; after an
# Ending the pages show what PLAY starts with; a bar's first chord a little late lands on its downbeat (writing in
# time, a new loop's take); REC says "REC: STOP" while it records; a lead counts in, stops with the song, starts at
# SONG's cursor row when armed, and copies a row's notes (one undo step).
# Funk: 100 BPM, a beat 600 ms, a bar 2400 ms. L1 (Pop): C G Am F, a bar each. Keys (octave 0): key K is MIDI 53 + K:
# Am 4 7 11, Dm 9 12 16, Em 11 14 18, C4 7, E4 11, G4 14.
wait 300
turn K1 1
expect tempo 100
# ---- L1 (4 bars) over Funk's Main A (2 bars). SEQ, REC armed: the footer offers 4 bars, SEL makes it so: bars 1-2
# repeated into 3-4 (the drums, the bass, the comping go on), a user pattern of the song's own (P01)
press HOME
tapkey w0
release HOME
tap SEQ
expect slot1_bars 2
expect slot1_trk1_count 44
expect slot1_trk4_count 18
tap REC
wait 50
expect recording 1
expect footer_is_SEL:_4_BARS,_AS_THE_LOOP|REC:_STOP 1
wait 100
shot rec_bars_hint.png
tap SEL
expect list_open 0
expect slot1_bars 4
expect song1_style1 0
expect slot1_trk1_count 88
expect slot1_trk4_count 36
expect msgtext_is_BARS_4_AS_THE_LOOP 1
expect recording 1
wait 100
shot rec_bars_done.png
tap REC
wait 50
expect recording 0
expect footer_is_KEYS:_C1_CLAVINET|REC:_RECORD 1
# ---- BARS while the loop plays: at the loop's bar 3 the pattern is at its bar 3; shorter (2): its bar 1; longer again
# (the notes kept past the end come back, nothing repeated over them): bar 4 at the loop's bar 4
tap PLAY
wait 5400
expect bar 2
turn SELECT 1
turn K1 -2
expect slot1_bars 2
wait 50
expect bar 0
turn K1 2
expect slot1_bars 4
expect slot1_trk1_count 88
wait 2400
expect loop_beat 13
expect bar 3
shot bars_in_step.png
# ---- an Ending (HOME + black key 5) plays out and stops: the pages show Main A again (what PLAY starts with), bar 1
press HOME
tapkey b4
release HOME
expect next_sect 6
wait 2400
expect sect 6
wait 7000
expect playing 0
expect sect 2
expect bar 0
turn SELECT -1
expect page 6
wait 100
shot after_ending_seq.png
# ---- writing chords in time (REC on HOME in LOOP, then PLAY): Dm 300 ms into bar 2 (its first chord, late): bar 2's
# downbeat (beat 4), not beat 5; Em 350 ms after bar 3's beat 2 (not a first beat): the nearest beat, 3.3 (beat 10)
tap HOME
expect page 0
tap REC
expect rec_chords 1
expect footer_is_KEYS:_CHORDS|REC:_STOP 1
tap PLAY
wait 2620
key 9 down
key 12 down
key 16 down
wait 100
key 9 up
key 12 up
key 16 up
wait 2924
key 11 down
key 14 down
key 18 down
wait 100
key 11 up
key 14 up
key 18 up
wait 300
expect loop_ch1_4 216
expect loop_ch1_5 -1
expect loop_ch1_10 416
tap REC
expect rec_chords 0
expect footer_is_KEYS:_CHORDS|REC:_WRITE 1
tap PLAY
wait 300
# ---- a new loop's take (FREE: KNOB 4 to "-"; REC while playing): counted in, "RECORDING NEW LOOP L9", the tag NEW
# LOOP L9 (not FREE), REC: STOP; Am a little late on its first downbeat: beat 0 (not 1)
turn K4 -16
expect mode 0
tap PLAY
key 4 down
key 7 down
key 11 down
wait 100
key 4 up
key 7 up
key 11 up
wait 300
tap REC
expect take 2
expect msgtext_is_RECORDING_NEW_LOOP_L9 1
expect tag_is_NEW_LOOP_L9 1
expect footer_is_KEYS:_CHORDS|REC:_STOP 1
wait 600
shot take_countin.png
wait 1528
key 4 down
key 7 down
key 11 down
wait 100
key 4 up
key 7 up
key 11 up
wait 2288
key 0 down
key 4 down
key 7 down
wait 100
key 0 up
key 4 up
key 7 up
wait 2288
tap REC
expect take 0
expect loop_ch9_0 916
expect loop_ch9_1 -1
expect loop_ch9_4 500
tap PLAY
wait 300
# ---- a song of two rows of L1 (white key 1 twice), row 1 on Main B (the other follows); INTRO off; PLAY: it plays to
# its Ending and stops: SEQ shows row 1's section (Main B), not the Ending
tap HOME
turn SELECT 1
expect page 1
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
expect rows 2
spin K1 -2
expect cursor 1
spin K3 2
expect row_sect1 2
turn SELECT 2
spin K1 -1
expect song_intro 0
expect song_ending 1
turn SELECT -2
tap PLAY
wait 19500
expect sect 6
shot song_ending.png
wait 6000
expect playing 0
expect sect 3
expect cursor 1
# ---- LD1, armed stopped with SONG's cursor on row 2: PLAY starts row 2 and records from its downbeat
spin K1 1
expect cursor 2
tap EDIT
turn ALGO 4
expect lead_sel 1
tap REC
expect recording 1
expect msgtext_is_RECORD_LD1_INTO_THE_SONG 1
wait 100
shot lead_armed_row2.png
tap PLAY
expect playing 1
expect row 2
wait 520
key 7 down
wait 300
key 7 up
wait 300
key 11 down
wait 300
key 11 up
wait 600
expect lead_count1_2 2
# the song stops: REC goes off with it
tap PLAY
wait 50
expect playing 0
expect recording 0
expect msgtext_is_RECORD_OFF_SONG_STOPPED 1
# ---- REC while the song plays: a count-in to the next bar line (a key before it only sounds)
tap PLAY
expect row 1
wait 1000
tap REC
wait 50
expect recording 1
expect rec_wait 1
wait 100
shot lead_countin.png
key 14 down
wait 200
key 14 up
wait 1200
expect rec_wait 0
expect lead_count1_1 0
wait 300
key 14 down
wait 200
key 14 up
wait 600
expect lead_count1_1 1
tap REC
wait 50
tap PLAY
wait 100
expect cursor 1
# ---- SEL's list (on its first action: ERASE LD1 IN ROW 1): COPY LD1 TO ROW 1 from row 2 (it has a note: asked)
tap SEL
expect list_sel 4
wait 100
shot lead_list.png
spin SELECT 3
expect list_sel 7
tap SEL
expect asking 1
wait 100
shot lead_copy_ask.png
tap SEL
expect asking 0
expect lead_count1_1 2
expect lead_count1_2 2
expect msgtext_is_COPIED_LD1_ROW_2_>_ROW_1 1
# one step: undone, redone
press HOME
tap REC
release HOME
expect lead_count1_1 1
expect msgtext_is_UNDO_COPY_LD1 1
press HOME
tap PLAY
release HOME
expect lead_count1_1 2
